---
// Project: occupant behavior in BIM-to-BEM workflows. Type: schema tree (data structure).
// Idea, Building Simulation 2025 abstract: "154 systematic enhancements to the existing occupant behavior XML (obXML)
// schema v1.3.4 ... to address existing limitations and improve interoperability with BIM models" (the count is not drawn).
// Labels and sources:
//   element names and nesting     Figs. 3 and 4; obXML_v1.4.xsd in the gb-obXML-Converter repository (root OccupantBehavior
//                                  with Buildings, Occupants, Behaviors, Zones, Schedules; Building with Area, Spaces,
//                                  BuildingStorey; Space with HVACConditionType, Systems; Systems with HVAC, Fans, Lights,
//                                  Windows, Doors and more; Schedules with Schedule, WeekSchedule, DaySchedule)
//   + new in v1.4                 4.1.1: Systems "expanded to include child elements for Fans and Doors"; "A new BuildingStorey
//                                  element is added"; "The Area element is introduced"; "HVACConditionType was added to the Space
//                                  element"; "the Zone element is newly introduced"; the schedule hierarchy "directly adopted"
//   filled from gbXML (dots)      5.3.2: Building ("mapped the Campus/Building element"), Area ("total floor area", space areas),
//                                  BuildingStorey ("preserving BuildingStorey references"), Space ("Space identification was
//                                  preserved"), HVACConditionType ("mapped from the conditionType attributes"), Systems ("a
//                                  dedicated Systems element under each Space"), Zones ("thermal design parameters in zones")
//   OB models                     the paper's "occupant behavior (OB)"; Occupants and Behaviors are the existing obXML part
// Collapsed to fit: "HVAC Lights Windows" lists three of the Systems children (PlugLoad, Thermostats and ShadesAndBlinds are
// not shown); "Schedule, Week/DaySchedule" stands for Schedule, WeekSchedule and DaySchedule; Area also sits under Space.
// Fine-line drawing (classes .dgf in global.css), in the 300 x 356 frame shared by the four project drawings.
---
